# [GAIA](../wg/gaia.html)

## Summary

The Global Access to the Internet for All (GAIA) Working Group met at IETF 121. The session featured five technical presentations covering community network deployments in rural India, reinforcement learning approaches for fine-grained Internet outage detection, open-source GIS tools for mapping population and connectivity, P2P network architectures for distributed AI agents, and active measurement frameworks for permissionless networks. The working group also reviewed the publication status of its ongoing draft on circular economies.

